[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5890657491","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123960#issuecomment-5890657491","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123960","id":5890657491,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABXxxM0w","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-29T12:50:29Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T12:54:38Z","body":"Interesting. Not come across this before.\r\n\r\nThe zero-fill regions are widely supported apparently, but with `static inline` or templated definitions across multiple compilation units it worries about \"One Definition Rule\" violations so it plays it safe and puts it in the .data section rather than .bss section.\r\n\r\nBTW this helps especially on multi-architecture \"universal\" builds apparently, because if there's a fat binary (say for 2 architectures), you don't need to put this zeroed data in either (in the binary), it only gets instantiated in 1 at runtime.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5890657491/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5892288587","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123960#issuecomment-5892288587","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123960","id":5892288587,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABXzUwSw","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-29T14:27:03Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T14:27:03Z","body":"Is this a macOS-specific thing? Given that Mach-O is mentioned above, I assume so. Or, at least an LLVM-specific thing given the link to LLVM in the comments?\r\n\r\nAnyway, a reduction of 512kb is great, and it'd be so cool to see that much fall off all builds :-)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5892288587/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"perfor